  "problem": {
    "id": "train-6309",
    "question": "Maddox and Theo both bought 3 Polaroid Cameras, each sold at $20 per camera from Amazon, and decided to sell them on eBay. Maddox sold his cameras at $28 each, while Theo sold his cameras at $23 each. How much more profit did Maddox get from the sale of his cameras than Theo?",
    "gold": "15",
    "answer": "The total cost of buying 3 cameras from Amazon for both Maddox and Theo was 3*$20=$<<3*20=60>>60\nMaddox sold his cameras at $28 each, for a total of $28*3=$<<28*3=84>>84\nMaddox made a profit of $84-$60=$<<84-60=24>>24 from the sale of his cameras.\nTheo sold his cameras on eBay for $23*3=$<<23*3=69>>69\nTheo made a profit of $69-$60=$<<69-60=9>>9\nMaddox made $24-$9=$15 more profit than Theo from the sale of his cameras.\n#### 15"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much more profit Maddox made compared to Theo, we need to calculate the profit for each of them and then find the difference.\n\nFirst, let's calculate Maddox's profit:\n1. Maddox bought 3 cameras at $20 each, so the total cost for Maddox is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 20 = 60 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n2. Maddox sold each camera for $28, so the total revenue from selling the cameras is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 28 = 84 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n3. Maddox's profit is the total revenue minus the total cost:\n   \\[\n   84 - 60 = 24 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate Theo's profit:\n1. Theo bought 3 cameras at $20 each, so the total cost for Theo is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 20 = 60 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n2. Theo sold each camera for $23, so the total revenue from selling the cameras is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 23 = 69 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n3. Theo's profit is the total revenue minus the total cost:\n   \\[\n   69 - 60 = 9 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nNow, we find the difference between Maddox's profit and Theo's profit:\n\\[\n24 - 9 = 15 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Maddox made \\(\\boxed{15}\\) dollars more than Theo.",
